From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] LYPython: drop pip's -e flag when INSTALLED_ENGINE is true

When a user project's `cmake configure` runs against a system-installed
engine at /opt/o3de, the engine source directory is read-only. O3DE's
ly_pip_install_local_package_editable function does `pip install -e` on
several Tools/* and scripts/o3de packages, and editable installs write
.egg-info directories next to the package's setup.py. That fails on a
read-only engine root with `Permission denied`.

Drop the `-e` flag when INSTALLED_ENGINE is set. Plain `pip install
<dir>` builds in a temp directory, so no source modifications are
needed. The semantic difference (editable vs pinned) doesn't matter
for an installed engine because the engine source can't change anyway.

This patch goes away on the day O3DE upstream adopts the same gate.
---
--- a/cmake/LYPython.cmake	2026-04-30 00:50:55.719478155 -0500
+++ b/cmake/LYPython.cmake	2026-04-30 00:50:44.729859260 -0500
@@ -267,8 +267,17 @@
 
     # now install the new one:
 
+    # When running against an installed (read-only) engine, drop the -e flag
+    # because editable installs write .egg-info into the source directory and
+    # /opt/o3de is read-only. Plain pip install builds in a temp dir.
+    if (INSTALLED_ENGINE)
+        set(_pip_install_mode_args "")
+    else()
+        set(_pip_install_mode_args "-e")
+    endif()
+
     execute_process(COMMAND 
-        ${LY_PYTHON_CMD} -m pip install -e ${package_folder_path} --no-deps --disable-pip-version-check  --no-warn-script-location 
+        ${LY_PYTHON_CMD} -m pip install ${_pip_install_mode_args} ${package_folder_path} --no-deps --disable-pip-version-check  --no-warn-script-location 
         WORKING_DIRECTORY ${LY_ROOT_FOLDER}/python
         RESULT_VARIABLE PIP_RESULT
         OUTPUT_VARIABLE PIP_OUT 
